        },
        "subject": "LU-20229 kernel: disable CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_AEAD",
        "message": "LU-20229 kernel: disable CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_AEAD\n\nThe most current kernels for RHEL 8.10, 9.7, and 10.1\ncontain the fix for the CVE-2026-31431 \"Copy Fail\" issue.\nHowever, old kernels do not have this fix. We need to\ndisable the CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_AEAD option at\nkernel-config level to mitigate the issue.\n\nAdditional related options commonly disabled for hardening are:\n\nCONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API\nCONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH\nCONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER\nCONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_RNG\n\nChange-Id: I84cfb2dd8fc74cf9120f13ca855f284f58209d30\nSigned-off-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
